.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_d2i ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_d2i_ex ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_i2d ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_new_func ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_new_ex_func ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_free_func ,
.Nm ASN1_ex_print_func ,
.Nm IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
.Nd ASN.1 external function support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1t.h
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_d2i
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const unsigned char **in"
.Fa "long len"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "int tag"
.Fa "int aclass"
.Fa "char opt"
.Fa "ASN1_TLC *ctx"
.Fc
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_d2i_ex
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const unsigned char **in"
.Fa "long len"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "int tag"
.Fa "int aclass"
.Fa "char opt"
.Fa "ASN1_TLC *ctx"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_i2d
.Fa "const ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "unsigned char **out"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "int tag"
.Fa "int aclass"
.Fc
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_new_func
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_new_ex_func
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft typedef void
.Fo ASN1_ex_free_func
.Fa "ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "const ASN1_ITEM *it"
.Fc
.Ft typedef int
.Fo ASN1_ex_print_func
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "const ASN1_VALUE **pval"
.Fa "int indent"
.Fa "const char *fname"
.Fa "const ASN1_PCTX *pctx"
.Fc
.Ft struct ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS_st {
    void *app_data;
    ASN1_ex_new_func *asn1_ex_new;
    ASN1_ex_free_func *asn1_ex_free;
    ASN1_ex_free_func *asn1_ex_clear;
    ASN1_ex_d2i *asn1_ex_d2i;
    ASN1_ex_i2d *asn1_ex_i2d;
    ASN1_ex_print_func *asn1_ex_print;
    ASN1_ex_new_ex_func *asn1_ex_new_ex;
    ASN1_ex_d2i_ex *asn1_ex_d2i_ex;
 };
 typedef struct ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS_st ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS;

 #define
.Fo IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
.Fa sname
.Fa tag
.Fa fptrs
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
ASN.1 data structures templates are typically defined in OpenSSL using a
series of macros such as
.Xr ASN1_SEQUENCE 3 ,
.Xr ASN1_SEQUENCE_END 3
and so on.
Instead templates can also be defined based entirely on external
functions.
These external functions are called to perform operations such as
creating a new
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
or converting an
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
to or from DER encoding.
.Pp
The macro
.Fn IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
can be used to create such an externally defined structure.
The name of the structure should be supplied in the
.Vt sname
parameter.
The tag for the structure (e.g.
typically
.Sy V_ASN1_SEQUENCE )
should be supplied in the
.Vt tag
parameter.
Finally a pointer to an
.Sy ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS
structure should be supplied in the
.Vt fptrs
parameter.
.Pp
The
.Sy ASN1_EXTERN_FUNCS
structure has the following entries.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Em app_data
A pointer to arbitrary application specific data.
.It Em asn1_ex_new
A "new" function responsible for constructing a new
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
object.
The newly constructed value should be stored in
.Em *pval .
The
.Fa it
parameter is a pointer to the
.Sy ASN1_ITEM
template object created via the
.Fn IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
macro.
.Pp
Returns a positive value on success or 0 on error.
.It Em asn1_ex_free
A "free" function responsible for freeing the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
passed in
.Em *pval
that was previously allocated via a "new" function.
The
.Fa it
parameter is a pointer to the
.Sy ASN1_ITEM
template object created via the
.Fn IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
macro.
.It Em asn1_ex_clear
A "clear" function responsible for clearing any data in the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
passed in
.Em *pval
and making it suitable for reuse.
The
.Fa it
parameter is a pointer to the
.Sy ASN1_ITEM
template object created via the
.Fn IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
macro.
.It Em asn1_ex_d2i
A "d2i" function responsible for converting DER data with the tag
.Vt tag
and class
.Em class
into an
.Vt ASN1_VALUE .
If
.Em *pval
is non-NULL then the
.Sy ASN_VALUE
it points to should be reused.
Otherwise a new
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
should be allocated and stored in
.Em *pval .
.Em *in
points to the DER data to be decoded and
.Fa len
is the length of that data.
After decoding
.Em *in
should be updated to point at the next byte after the decoded data.
If the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
is considered optional in this context then
.Fa opt
will be nonzero.
Otherwise it will be zero.
The
.Fa it
parameter is a pointer to the
.Sy ASN1_ITEM
template object created via the
.Fn IMPLEMENT_EXTERN_ASN1
macro.
A pointer to the current
.Vt ASN1_TLC
context (which may be required for other ASN1 function calls) is passed
in the
.Fa ctx
parameter.
.Pp
The
.Em asn1_ex_d2i
entry may be NULL if
.Em asn1_ex_d2i_ex
has been specified instead.
.Pp
Returns <= 0 on error or a positive value on success.
.It Em asn1_ex_i2d
An "i2d" function responsible for converting an
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
into DER encoding.
On entry
.Em *pval
will contain the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
to be encoded.
If default tagging is to be used then
.Vt tag
will be -1 on entry.
Otherwise if implicit tagging should be used then
.Vt tag
and
.Fa aclass
will be the tag and associated class.
.Pp
If
.Fa out
is not NULL then this function should write the DER encoded data to the
buffer in
.Em *out ,
and then increment
.Em *out
to point to immediately after the data just written.
.Pp
If
.Fa out
is NULL then no data should be written but the length calculated and
returned as if it were.
.Pp
The
.Em asn1_ex_i2d
entry may be NULL if
.Em asn1_ex_i2d_ex
has been specified instead.
.Pp
The return value should be negative if a fatal error occurred, or 0 if a
non-fatal error occurred.
Otherwise it should return the length of the encoded data.
.It Em asn1_ex_print
A "print" function.
.Fa out
is the BIO to print the output to.
.Em *pval
is the
.Vt ASN1_VALUE
to be printed.
.Fa indent
is the number of spaces of indenting to be printed before any data is
printed.
.Fa fname
is currently unused and is always "".
.Fa pctx
is a pointer to the
.Sy ASN1_PCTX
for the print operation.
.Pp
Returns 0 on error or a positive value on success.
If the return value is 2 then an additional newline will be printed
after the data printed by this function.
.It Em asn1_ex_new_ex
This is the same as
.Em asn1_ex_new
except that it is additionally passed the OSSL_LIB_CTX to be used in
.Fa libctx
and any property query string to be used for algorithm fetching in the
.Fa propq
parameter.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further details.
If
.Em asn1_ex_new_ex
is non NULL, then it will always be called in preference to
.Em asn1_ex_new .
.It Em asn1_ex_d2i_ex
This is the same as
.Em asn1_ex_d2i
except that it is additionally passed the OSSL_LIB_CTX to be used in
.Fa libctx
and any property query string to be used for algorithm fetching in the
.Fa propq
parameter.
See
.Xr crypto 7
for further details.
If
.Em asn1_ex_d2i_ex
is non NULL, then it will always be called in preference to
.Em asn1_ex_d2i .
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Return values for the various callbacks are as described above.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ASN1_item_new_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Em asn1_ex_new_ex
and
.Em asn1_ex_d2i_ex
callbacks were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
